Package: hybdiv
Type: Package
Title: Hybrid Selection Under a Molecular Diversity Constraint
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Eder", "D. B. S.", email = "ederdbs@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for selecting a subset of F1 hybrids that maximises a
    multi-trait genomic index while constraining the loss of molecular gene
    diversity relative to a same-size random-sampling baseline. Provides the
    Caballero and Toro molecular coancestry kernel, a catalogue of diversity
    metrics sharing a single signature, selection strategies (truncation,
    greedy, differential evolution, local search with parallel tempering,
    a rounded optimal-contribution relaxation and an exact outer-approximation
    oracle), and a segregating-population sizing simulator for wide
    biparental crosses.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0)
Imports:
